{"agent_id":"pp3g-DgPP-research-read-only-do-not-modify-files-produce-a-full","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T05:37:35.111074839Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"de06e91e-ec85-4cb8-8720-2a04f8d8c830","comment_uuid":"ef64cb90-a0fd-4019-9b30-5ad431fa9e31","author":"pp3g-DgPP-research-read-only-do-not-modify-files-produce-a-full","content":"## Agent Orchestration Playbook — Full Rule Inventory & Hookability Classification\n\n**Source:** .crosslink/knowledge/agent-orchestration-playbook.md (825 lines)\n**Date:** 2026-08-18\n**Purpose:** Exhaustive inventory of every rule, mandate, procedure, and anti-pattern, classified by hookability for a proposed documentation-check-before-consequential-action hook.\n\n### Existing Hook Infrastructure\n\n| Mechanism | File | What it enforces today |\n|-----------|------|----------------------|\n| OpenCode plugin | crosslink-guard.ts | Blocked git commands, gated git (active issue), comment discipline, active-issue enforcement, kill/pause flags, allowed bash |\n| OpenCode plugin | orchestrator-guard.ts | Write/edit blocked for non-Builder agents |\n| OpenCode plugin | rtk-guard.ts | Transparent RTK command rewriting |\n| Claude Code hook | heartbeat.py | Agent heartbeats on 120s throttle |\n| Claude Code hook | crosslink_config.py | Shared config, crosslink binary resolution |\n\n---\n\n### §1 Division of Labor\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 1.1 Orchestrator never implements | **Partial** | (a) OpenCode plugin | **ALREADY ENFORCED** by orchestrator-guard.ts + crosslink-guard.ts narrow bash allowlist |\n| 1.2 Orchestrator never reviews own work | **No** | — | Requires semantic judgment about synthesis vs rubber-stamping |\n| 1.3 Workers never plan/review/merge to master | **Partial** | (a) OpenCode plugin | **ALREADY ENFORCED**: task deny + git push/merge blocked |\n\n### §2 Choose Your Tier\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 2.1 Do not swarm what kickoff can do | **No** | — | Complexity judgment |\n| 2.2 Do not kickoff multi-phase serially | **No** | — | Same |\n| 2.3 Prove serially, then fan out | **No** | — | Pattern-maturity judgment |\n| 2.4 Task tool NOT orchestration tier | **Partial** | Task permission allowlist | **Partially enforced**; cannot detect intent |\n| 2.5 NEVER use Task for implementation | **Partial** | Same | Same limitation |\n| 2.6 NEVER use Task for review verdicts | **No** | — | Semantic |\n| 2.7 NEVER use Task for durable trail | **No** | — | Semantic |\n\n### §3 Model Selection\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 3.1 Every kickoff/swarm MUST include --model | **Yes** | (a) OpenCode plugin — regex check on bash calls | **NOT ENFORCED — HIGH PRIORITY GAP** |\n| 3.2 Verify model against live catalog | **Partial** | (c) crosslink CLI | Adds ~1-2s latency |\n| 3.3 Pass --model explicitly | **Yes** | Same as 3.1 | Same |\n| 3.4 HALT if model unreachable | **Partial** | Runtime check needed | Cannot detect network unreachability |\n| 3.5 Free Zen caution | **Partial** | Warn on opencode/ prefix | Cannot detect rate limits |\n| 3.6 Block legacy claude-mode wrappers | **Yes** | (a) prefix match | Low priority |\n\n### §4 Pre-Flight Checklist\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 4.1 HEAD clean and on expected branch | **Partial** | (a) git status check before dispatch | ~100ms cost |\n| 4.2 Target model accessible | **Partial** | Same as 3.2 | Same trade-off |\n| 4.3 Crosslink issue exists and claimed | **Yes** | (a) sentinel file check | Partially enforced via --issue requirement |\n| 4.4 Worktree clean (no orphan .kickoff-status) | **Partial** | (c) filesystem scan | Trivial |\n| 4.5 Feature branch does not already exist | **Partial** | (c) git branch check | Trivial |\n| 4.6 Prompt includes acceptance criteria | **No** | — | NLP required |\n\n### §5.1 Single-Agent Kickoff\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 5.1.1 Command must include --model, --issue, --verify, --timeout | **Yes** | (a) regex arg check | **NOT ENFORCED — HIGH PRIORITY** |\n| 5.1.2 Print tmux attach command | **No** | Output format rule | |\n| 5.1.3 Record dispatch breadcrumb | **No** | Cannot force action | |\n| 5.1.4 Do NOT poll obsessively | **No** | Temporal judgment | |\n| 5.1.5 Watch for missing checkpoints | **Partial** | (c) existing watcher | Partially addressed |\n\n### §5.2 Swarm Rules\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 5.2.1 One phase at a time, gate between phases | **Partial** | (c) crosslink CLI | Requires fork modification |\n| 5.2.2 Budget windows are hard limits | **Yes** | (c) timeout enforcement | Partially enforced |\n| 5.2.3 blocked_by edges as process gate | **No** | — | Human verification |\n\n### §5.3 Task-Matched Timeouts\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 5.3.1 Timeouts MUST be task-matched — never blanket 1h | **Yes** | (a) reject --timeout 1h/60m | **NOT ENFORCED — HIGH PRIORITY** |\n| 5.3.2 Task-type ceiling guidance | **Partial** | (a) warn if >45m, suggest swarm | Heuristic |\n| 5.3.3 Two-signal stalled detection | **Partial** | (d) existing watcher + git-log polling | Partially addressed |\n\n### §5.4 Progress-Feedback Contract\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 5.4.1 Post checkpoints at milestones | **Partial** | (c) post-hoc audit at session end | Cannot force real-time posting |\n| 5.4.2 Durability cadence (~5-min) | **Partial** | (c) position staleness detection | Partially via watcher |\n| 5.4.3 Structured checkpoint fields | **Partial** | (c) regex validation | Trivial |\n| 5.4.4 Sync after posting | **Partial** | (c) auto-sync after observation | Requires fork modification |\n| 5.4.5 Missed check-in escalation | **Partial** | Same as 5.3.3 | |\n| 5.4.6 Task-awareness (trivial midpoint optional) | **No** | — | Requires knowing task type |\n| 5.4.7 Session actions are supplementary only | **No** | — | Semantic distinction |\n\n### §5.5 Two-Repo Sync\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 5.5.1 Changes to shared files must be mirrored | **No** | — | Cross-repo coordination |\n| 5.5.2 Durability-cadence changes must be mirrored | **No** | — | Same |\n\n### §5.6 Reviewer Independence\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 5.6.1 Each reviewer on own sub-issue | **Partial** | (c) validate isolated sub-issues | Requires fork modification |\n| 5.6.2 Never multiple reviewers on one thread | **Partial** | (a) count reviewer subagents per issue | Requires tracking |\n| 5.6.3 Orchestrator synthesizes after all verdicts | **No** | — | Semantic timing |\n\n### §5.7 Thin-Orchestrator Rule\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 5.7.1 Bounded signals only — large reads delegated | **Partial** | (a) command length/complexity limits | Heuristic |\n| 5.7.2 Never paste large raw output | **No** | — | Context volume |\n| 5.7.3 Pipe-chain gotcha | **Partial** | (a) detect | in orchestrator bash | Trivial regex |\n\n### §5.8 Workflow Topology\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 5.8.1 Structured position updates | **Partial** | (c) validate format | Post-hoc |\n| 5.8.2 Certainty disclosure for cross-role claims | **No** | — | NLP required |\n| 5.8.3 First position within ~2 min | **Partial** | (c) timestamp check | Post-hoc audit |\n| 5.8.4 Position at every state transition + ~5 min | **Partial** | Same as 5.4.2 | |\n| 5.8.5 completed claims carry artifact link | **Partial** | (c) regex for URL/hash | Trivial |\n| 5.8.6 Phase-1 auditor alongside builder | **No** | — | Dispatch composition |\n| 5.8.7 Phase-2 auditor model-varied | **No** | — | Model comparison |\n| 5.8.8 Review-before-consume gate | **Partial** | (c) enforce reviewer verdict before close | Partially done |\n| 5.8.9 Pre-positioned AUDITOR | **No** | — | Dispatch composition |\n| 5.8.10 Cheap staleness trigger | **Partial** | Same as 5.4.2 | Via existing watcher |\n| 5.8.11 Claim-vs-artifact mismatch detection | **Partial** | (c) regex heuristic | False positives likely |\n| 5.8.12 Orchestrator as single integration point | **No** | — | Architectural |\n\n### §5.9 Decision-Gating Build Artifacts\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 5.9.1 Artifacts MUST be committed before session end | **Partial** | (c) pre-close /tmp scan | Post-hoc audit |\n| 5.9.2 /tmp is scratch, not home | **Partial** | Same | Warning only |\n| 5.9.3 Closeout checklist | **Partial** | (c) session end pre-flight | Requires fork modification |\n| 5.9.4 Cleanup guards preserve uncommitted state | **Partial** | (c) pre-cleanup check | Requires fork modification |\n\n### §6.1 Status Checks\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 6.1.1 Never trust status flags alone | **No** | — | Already via watcher |\n| 6.1.2 Durable primitive is ground truth | **No** | — | Guidance |\n| 6.1.3 Checkpoints are progress signal | **No** | — | Guidance |\n| 6.1.4 Distinguish STALLED from WORKING via ps | **Partial** | Same as watcher | Already addressed |\n\n### §6.2 Output Verification\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 6.2.1 Verify output non-empty | **Partial** | (c) length check | Trivial |\n| 6.2.2 Deterministic verification only | **No** | — | Safety-critical classification |\n| 6.2.3 Build from main checkout | **No** | — | Build semantics |\n| 6.2.4 Verify against hub refs not local DB | **No** | — | Already via durable fix |\n\n### §6.3 Micro-Gate\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 6.3.1 Review before close | **Partial** | (c) enforce result comment | Partially done |\n| 6.3.2 FAIL → fix and re-review | **No** | — | Semantic |\n| 6.3.3 Empty/silent review → CRASH | **Partial** | (c) empty output check | **NOT ENFORCED — HIGH PRIORITY** |\n\n### §6.4 Agent Lifecycle Watcher\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 6.4.1-6.4.4 Full lifecycle monitoring | **Yes** | (d) systemd + kickoff-notify.py | **ALREADY IMPLEMENTED** |\n\n### §6.5 Hub Refs Ground Truth\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 6.5.1 Read hub refs not local DB | **No** | — | Already via fix |\n| 6.5.2 Never blind-sync in main repo | **Partial** | (a) CWD check + warn | Trivial |\n| 6.5.3 Liveness ≠ visibility | **No** | — | Guidance |\n\n### §6.6 Standing Workflow\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 6.6.1 Agent Status note every turn | **No** | — | Cannot force output |\n| 6.6.2 Cleanup after dispatch waves | **Partial** | (c) reminder | Cannot force execution |\n| 6.6.3 Watcher is supplement not substitute | **No** | — | Guidance |\n\n### §7 Failure Protocol\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 7.1 STOP on delegation failure — no retry/substitute/self-exec | **Partial** | (a) detect retry patterns | Heuristic |\n| 7.2 Report failure clearly | **No** | — | Semantic |\n| 7.3 REMAIN HALTED until operator | **Partial** | (a) set halted flag, block tools | State management needed |\n| 7.4 Violating HALT = role breach | **No** | — | Consequence rule |\n\n### §7.1 Crash Recovery\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 7.1.1-7.1.3 ps/kill/confirm | **No** | — | Manual procedure |\n| 7.1.4 Re-assert signing key | **Partial** | (c) auto in session start | Fork modification |\n| 7.1.5 Cleanup --force | **Partial** | (c) reminder | Already exists |\n| 7.1.6 Relaunch from hub + git log | **No** | — | Human judgment |\n\n### §8 Signing Key Discipline\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 8.1 Re-assert key before kickoff/cleanup/crash | **Partial** | (c) auto in session start/kickoff | Fork modification |\n| 8.2 Verify signingkey after re-assertion | **Partial** | (c) post-assertion check | Fork modification |\n| 8.3 Workers rewriting signing config | **Partial** | (c) git-log audit | Post-hoc |\n\n### §9 Worktree/Branch Management\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 9.1 Workers commit to feature branches only | **Yes** | **ALREADY ENFORCED** by crosslink-guard.ts | |\n| 9.2 Push is operator-gated | **Yes** | **ALREADY ENFORCED** by crosslink-guard.ts | |\n| 9.3 Orchestrator merge gated on active issue | **Yes** | **ALREADY ENFORCED** by crosslink-guard.ts | |\n| 9.4 Worktree overlap merge order | **No** | — | File dependency graph |\n| 9.5 One scope per session | **No** | — | Semantic |\n\n### §9.1 Operator Git Convention\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 9.1.1 --no-edit on operator git commands | **Partial** | (a) inject --no-edit or warn | Command mutation |\n| 9.1.2 core.editor true safety net | **No** | — | User-side config |\n\n### §10 Gate Discipline\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 10.1-10.2 Workers commit, no push; merge gated | **Yes** | **ALREADY ENFORCED** | |\n| 10.3 Nothing merges unreviewed | **Partial** | (a) verify reviewer verdict before merge | Requires tracking |\n| 10.4 Fidelity-sensitive work held at gate | **No** | — | Judgment |\n\n### §11 Verification Asymmetry\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 11.1-11.3 Committed ≠ verified | **No** | — | Build semantics |\n\n### §12 Documentation and Handoff\n\n| Rule | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 12.1 Session end requires --notes | **Yes** | (c) reject without --notes | **NOT ENFORCED — HIGH PRIORITY** |\n| 12.2 Post milestone checkpoints | **Partial** | (c) post-hoc audit | Partially done |\n| 12.3 Breadcrumbs supplementary only | **No** | — | Same as 5.4.7 |\n| 12.4 Issue reference in commits [#N] | **Partial** | (a) regex on commit message | Trivial |\n| 12.5 Never edit STATUS.md directly | **Partial** | (a) file-path block | Trivial |\n| 12.6 Design prompts for rebuildability | **No** | — | Judgment |\n\n### §13 Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Hookable? | Mechanism | Notes |\n|-------------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| 13.1 Task tool for implementation | **Partial** | Task allowlist | Partially enforced |\n| 13.2 Omitting --model | **Yes** | Same as 3.1 | **HIGH PRIORITY GAP** |\n| 13.3 Blanket --timeout 1h | **Yes** | Same as 5.3.1 | **HIGH PRIORITY GAP** |\n| 13.4 claude-mode wrappers | **Yes** | Same as 3.6 | Low priority |\n| 13.5 Empty review output | **Partial** | Same as 6.3.3 | **HIGH PRIORITY GAP** |\n| 13.6 Orchestrator implementing | **Yes** | **ALREADY ENFORCED** | |\n| 13.7 Parallelizing unproven patterns | **No** | — | Judgment |\n| 13.8 Trusting .kickoff-status | **No** | — | Already via watcher |\n| 13.9 Waiting silently | **Partial** | Via existing watcher | |\n| 13.10 Session actions for visibility | **No** | — | Same as 5.4.7 |\n| 13.11 Multiple reviewers one thread | **Partial** | Same as 5.6.2 | |\n| 13.12 Merge to master from worktree | **Yes** | **ALREADY ENFORCED** | |\n| 13.13 Retrying failed delegation | **Partial** | Heuristic detection | |\n| 13.14 LLM sampling for safety gates | **No** | — | Classification |\n| 13.15 Pushing from orchestrator | **Yes** | **ALREADY ENFORCED** | |\n| 13.16 Trusting static permission doc | **No** | — | Meta-rule |\n| 13.17 Reading from local SQLite DB